---
// The trust points: "Nothing extra to pay" leads. Lookover runs on the person's computer only: the service
// listens on this machine alone, and there is no server mode yet (the README's "Security").
---

<section class="trust lined">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="grid3">
      <div class="rise">
        <h3 class="h4">Nothing extra to pay</h3>
        <p>Reviews use the Claude or ChatGPT plan you already have. No per-review price, no credits to buy, no seats.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rise">
        <h3 class="h4">Runs on your machine</h3>
        <p>On your computer. No account with us, no hosted service in between, no telemetry.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rise">
        <h3 class="h4">Never touches your logins</h3>
        <p>It runs the official <code>claude</code> and <code>codex</code> CLIs, signed in as you. It never reads or stores your tokens.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
